Peter- It's true. That's why I led off with "This question may be a little out of place here".

Quoting the ggvis page at rstudio, "The graphics produced by ggvis are fundamentally web graphics".  More generally, it seems to be the future all-purpose package at the head of a family of web based plotting tools within htmlwidgets.  Another one of those is leaflet.  For now, there isn't a google group for either of those, and I'm interested in a specific ggvis function - linked_brush - and I'm wondering about it's potential portability to its brothers and sisters, in this case, leaflet.

Some people reading this may know both packages.

Cheers and apologies.

